<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Cessetani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 218 BCE (approx.) · capital Kese</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Iberian people of the Tarragona area, in whose land the Romans probably won their first battle in Iberia, at Cissa in 218 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Cessetani, or Cosetani, inhabited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camp-de-tarragona">Camp de Tarragona</a> and the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penedes">Penedès</a> in southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a> from about the 5th century BCE. Their main settlement was Kese, usually located at or near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarragona">Tarragona</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their territory had fortified settlements such as Alorda Park at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calafell">Calafell</a> and lived from farming and trade along the coast. Kese minted widely circulated coins with an Iberian legend. Their political structure is not recorded, but they were prosperous enough for both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> to value the area.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 218 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-cornelius-scipio-calvus">Gnaeus Scipio</a> defeated the Carthaginian commander Hanno near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cissa">Cissa</a>, a town sometimes identified with Kese, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> established their base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a>. The region thus became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> first foothold in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, and Tarraco grew into the capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a> and later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hispania-tarraconensis">Tarraconensis</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cessetani.jpg" alt="Cessetani" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Bibliothèque nationale de France · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Denier,_argent,_Kese,_Ib%C3%A9rie_-_btv1b10301728w_(2_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 218 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kese</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iberian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cosetani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-359&amp;focus=cessetani" aria-label="Cessetani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4709 712 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cessetani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5029 968L5031 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5029 968h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5029 968h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kese. <a href="/atlas?year=-359&amp;focus=cessetani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
